    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16669" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">excē^tra</span></b> , ae, f.
		perh. corrupted from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχιδνα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a snake</i>, <i>serpent</i> (very
			rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop., <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Pers. 1, 1, 3 sq.</span></i>; * Cic. <b>poet.</b> Tusc. 2, 9, 22.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, a reproachful epithet for a bad,
			intriguing woman, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas. 3, 5, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Ps. 1,
				2, 82</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 39, 11</span></i>.</div>
